payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787027941603250001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c4dbb45c-86d5-4df9-b63f-56bfbcf03abc","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a8cd-01cd-c370-454f"},{"link_uuid":"d2abcca6-e3a2-429f-8534-59b2e4b9bfeb","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c"},{"link_uuid":"fe982632-4aad-4c5b-a49a-9fc9171f3dad","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a"},{"link_uuid":"60ab984d-bf68-43fb-8c39-f3e6b8b27fad","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ca70-6273-8d72-4812"},{"link_uuid":"f7b8a45f-0bbc-408c-8c3a-f8168ef49e1a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"26d8-0e82-dd19-465a"}],"description":"## Context\nCloud/DC atomic executors need a core route that bypasses generic retry without falsely advancing the current handler baseline. Production must remain on legacy until S3 validates and cuts over.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd a constructor-injected legacy-default selector for exact summary updates, map confirmed outcomes through the existing result surface, and expose terminal outcomes as bounded per-mutation errors without baseline/provenance advance. Finalize the S1 section of ADR 0103.\n\n## Plan\n1. Route only exact `{\"summary\"}` when tests explicitly enable the selector. Mixed fields remain one unsplit legacy call. Add no config/env key and never dual-send.\n2. Poison-test generic `_call_with_retry` on the selected route. Preserve every unselected route.\n3. SUCCESS cohort. The S1 T2/T3 summary executors emit `applied` and `recovered` on success; map both to the legacy successful-update result surface (`result={\"key\": jira_key}`, leaving `error`/`_comment_errors`/`_subop` as legacy success does) and advance the ADR-0026 baseline. Include `already_satisfied` in the success cohort as a DEFENSIVE/forward-compat no-op mapping — it is NOT currently emitted by the S1 executors, so pin it with a test asserting it advances the baseline identically. Because `OperationOutcome` carries NO field payload, the success route derives the value written to `_fields_synced`/`ctx.synced_fields` from the routed mutation's own `fields[\"summary\"]` (the string just sent), keyed by the mutation's `local_id`; that is what reaches the baseline advance and preserves byte-parity with the legacy `{\"key\": jira_key}` result surface.\n4. TERMINAL cohort. Map EVERY other disposition the executors can return — `commit_unknown`, `retryable_deferred`, `permanent_failure`, `exhausted_transient`, and any further non-success disposition (`dependency_deferred`, `scope_deferred`, `safety_aborted`, `skipped`) — identically as terminal: emit an internal tagged result consumed by `handle_update` that sets `result=None`, records exactly one redacted per-mutation error/disposition message capped at 512 Unicode code points, carries the OperationOutcome `retry_not_before` value (a RetryPlan field, not a disposition) onto the manifest for observability only, keeps `_fields_synced` empty, advances no baseline/provenance, persists no S1 deferral, and continues the batch.\n5. Name S3 as sole cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and bridge-retirement owner in contract/ADR.\n\n## Testing\nUse exact-versus-mixed routing tables, poison retries, Cloud/DC verified fakes, and apply-handler spies asserting one message, redaction, the 512-code-point boundary, and the derived-from-`fields[\"summary\"]` baseline value — across the success cohort (`applied`, `recovered`, and the defensive `already_satisfied`) and the terminal cohort (`commit_unknown`, `retryable_deferred`, and the 512/redaction boundary).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The internal selector defaults to legacy and adds no config or environment key.\n- [ ] Test-enabled exact summary bypasses generic retry, while mixed fields remain one legacy call.\n- [ ] The success dispositions `applied` and `recovered` (plus the defensive, not-currently-emitted `already_satisfied`) preserve all existing result and telemetry shapes and advance the baseline with the summary derived from the routed mutation's `fields[\"summary\"]`.\n- [ ] Every non-success disposition (`commit_unknown`, `retryable_deferred`, `permanent_failure`, `exhausted_transient`, and any further terminal disposition) records exactly one redacted per-mutation error/disposition message capped at 512 Unicode code points and never advances baseline or provenance.\n- [ ] Terminal outcomes persist no deferral in S1 and do not stop unrelated batch work.\n- [ ] ADR 0103 names S3 as sole production cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and compatibility-bridge retirement owner.\n\n## Out of scope\nDefault-on routing, fuse behavior, and durable deferral remain RP-03 S3.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/summary_route.py","reason":"New leaf module: the exact-{summary} selector predicate and the OperationOutcome→result/error/synced-baseline mapping, extracted from dispatch_one (at 740 LOC) to respect the 800-LOC cap; the executor is called directly so the selected route bypasses the generic retry wrapper."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Add the constructor-injected legacy-default summary_executor field to BatchApplyContext and the routing guard in handle_update that consumes terminal tags without false baseline/provenance advance."},{"path":"docs/adr/0103-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Finalize the S1 lifecycle boundary naming S3 as sole production cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and compatibility-bridge retirement owner."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py","reason":"Held-out oracle: exact-vs-mixed routing, generic-retry poison bypass, terminal outcome mapping (one redacted ≤512-codepoint message, no baseline/provenance advance, batch continues), and the ADR-0103 S3-ownership assertion."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a"],["depends_on","a8cd-01cd-c370-454f"],["depends_on","c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c"],["parent","f5ac-6373-5e33-4374"],["relates_to","26d8-0e82-dd19-465a"],["relates_to","ca70-6273-8d72-4812"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f5ac-6373-5e33-4374","parent_status_uuid":"1cb2deba-e3fd-4acf-8912-c68abad2f1e5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["rp03","retry","reconciler","tdd","adr"],"ticket_id":"72d0-0f09-1694-4010","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S1 T4 — Integrate the summary executor behind the legacy-default seam","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_retry.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Selector, routing, result compatibility, terminal error, and no false state advance"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"ADR lifecycle ownership and documentation index"}]},"source_event_uuids":["fe982632-4aad-4c5b-a49a-9fc9171f3dad","96d1ed37-72bd-4f57-9c0a-f00b94120fad","18e6d227-af1e-4afe-97d2-1ddf816d2c8f","12c468bc-85e2-4e84-b8d1-ab00abeb11ac","8c74787c-f894-4a0f-affe-a14a91bc1961","1cb2deba-e3fd-4acf-8912-c68abad2f1e5","d650f6bb-0858-45d9-b141-fbca18025310","a5a02ec4-5773-4264-aeb2